WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.160
"At around 3PM on July 31st,

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.360
a five-year-old boy fell off the
balcony of a third-floor apartment

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.400
in a Shimizu public housing complex.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.990
However, a passerby caught the boy,
preventing him from being seriously hurt,

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.740
and he escaped with only light injuries.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.610
The brave passerby was a high school girl,
who left without introducing herself.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:24.600
She was reportedly carrying an instrument case
and seemed to be in a rush."

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.890
Who am I? Where am I?

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.920
Your name is Homura Chika,

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.590
and this is the lobby of the City Cultural Hall.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:36.300
You can avert your eyes from reality,
but not your ears from what I'm about to say.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.380
Today's the day of the district qualifiers.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:43.190
So how's our brave high school girl doing?

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:52.360
I sprained my wrist, threw out my back,
and fainted once I got home.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.370
No playing in the lobby, please.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:34.260
Wow, quite the crowd we have here.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.790
But there's still time until the opening ceremony...

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:39.080
I'm starting to get nervous!

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.300
Where did your usual confidence go?

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.040
Lately, I've been messing up
when it matters most.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.370
Want me to write a calming charm on your palm?

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.710
Please do!

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.430
No! Don't abandon me!

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:52.320
Now that I've quit volleyball,
the flute is all I have!

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.230
I'd rather fall flat on my face
after the performance!

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.650
What are you talking about?

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.940
Oh, hello, everyone.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.400
I'm fine! I can do my best!

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.660
Sounds rough.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.540
Catching a five-year-old must've
hit you like a ton of bricks.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.090
How could you get hurt before the qualifiers?!

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.500
Can you play the flute?

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.920
You hadn't told them?

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.280
Why would I make them panic
first thing in the morning?

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.670
Why would you make them panic at the venue?!

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:24.220
Quit fighting, you two.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.710
Serizawa-san!

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:28.650
Show me your hand.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.480
You know what happened, Serizawa?

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.320
She and her mum came crying to me last night.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.280
My commiserations, Nao-chan.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.260
Nao-chan? What's up with that?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.660
They're childhood friends.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.910
So how's her injury?

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:48.010
Her wrist's a bit swollen,
but it shouldn't be a problem.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:51.000
And she already passed a playing test
on the riverbank late last night.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.910
She was messing up the exact
same parts as yesterday.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.520
I guess she's made of stern stuff.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.210
Wait, why do you know how
she was playing yesterday?

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.800
Wh-What does it matter?

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.690
I wish she'd hit her head and
been reborn as a flute virtuoso.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:09.170
Same here.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.400
What the heck?

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.810
You practised at the riverbank late last night?
Were you girls all right by yourselves?

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:16.770
We had Kamijou-kun come as well.

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:19.520
In fact, he's the one
I'm more worried about.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:20.230
And why is that?

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:23.270
He laughed when he heard
what happened to Homura-san,

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.990
and the two broke out into a scuffle.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.290
And here I thought a cat scratched him.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.950
A cute cat got you, didn't it?

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.640
It was a rowdy cat with bundles
of energy, if nothing else.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.580
Where've you been, Kamijou-kun?

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:44.090
Oh, I just found someone who was lost.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:47.590
Wow, Kamijou-senpai.
You're so relaxed before the performance.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.970
Aren't there a few too many reporters
for district qualifiers?

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:52.930
Yeah.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.860
Sorry about this. I'll sneak around like a ninja
so I don't cause trouble for the rest of you.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.150
They're probably not here for you.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.720
You reek.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.190
Have you been taking regular baths?

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.240
What're you talking about?

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.940
You reek of animal.

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.240
You're just smelling things.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.160
Must be hard living by yourself.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.630
Maybe I should go wash up in the canal outside.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.120
I seriously hope you're kidding.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:20.670
I am.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.510
By the way, isn't Kusakabe-sensei here yet?

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.420
No. The plan was to meet up at the venue...

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:33.390
Relax. Our performance is the
twenty-fifth out of twenty-six.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.360
Our instruments will be brought in at 2PM.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:36.900
Tuning starts at 2:30PM.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.770
Stand by backstage at 2:50PM.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.360
Performance starts at 3PM.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.660
You two are making me dizzy.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:47.860
If our instruments are only coming at 2PM,
why did we show up so early?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.980
Most of our members are making
their competition debuts today,

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:53.380
so it'll do them good to get
used to the atmosphere, right?

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.530
Oh, there you are.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:56.790
Sakai-sensei?

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:00.130
Congrats on making it through the
Category A qualifiers with flying colours.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:04.540
Well, our goal is to put on the greatest
performance at the All-Japans.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:08.130
Fujigasaki are taking part in today's
Category B qualifiers too, right?

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:11.460
I think I'm gonna become part
of the Fujigasaki family after all!

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:13.540
Hope you like having
a gorilla for an instructor.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.660
Okay, that would suck.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.010
I can hear you, you know.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.230
So you two are Homura and Kamijou?

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.320
Yes.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.370
Sorry about that.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:24.000
You two are just like the rumours say.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.060
What rumours?

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:28.230
That aside, I have a message
for you from Kusakabe-sensei.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:29.920
A message from Kusakabe-sensei?

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.860
Why would he ask you?

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.740
Because I contacted him.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.990
I wanted to ask him if you guys wanted
to use the practice space we're using.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.070
Can we?!

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:42.160
You sure can. Our performance is early in the order,
so it'll be empty in the afternoon.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:47.040
Apparently Kusakabe-sensei's running late
and will only get here at 1PM,

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:50.640
so he asked the president
to take charge until then.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.310
Got it!

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:57.800
Also, if you get interviewed about the competition,
you don't have to answer any questions.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:19.530
They came together perfectly at the start.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.850
Yeah. The brass instruments
were in perfect harmony too.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:25.670
I heard these guys only got
bronze last year, though.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.350
When they're this good?

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:31.130
We're not going to do worse than bronze, are we?

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.350
Huh? What're Shimizu Minami doing here?

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:35.660
I didn't know they even had a concert band.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.210
Well, now you do!

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:39.130
It's like we don't belong here.

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:40.670
Don't let it affect you.

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:44.350
We came here early in order
to get used to the atmosphere.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.440
Stay confident. Let's advance to the regionals.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.810
We don't want this to be the end, right?

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:50.590
Right!

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.280
Wait, where's Kamijou?

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.040
He went out earlier.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.210
He's been acting strange all day.

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:01.320
I'll go look for him!

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:03.340
Watch my bag and flute, Gotou-san.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:04.210
Roger!

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.190
Haruta...

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.010
Don't tell me...

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:18.470
he's seriously washing up here... or not.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:27.310
Huh? So pets are allowed here.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:32.490
A writer?

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.030
Freelance.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.670
Mind if I interview you for a story?

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:38.460
Please don't show my face!

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.640
I'm nobody important!

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:44.830
You're here to interview the
brave high school girl, right?

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:48.140
No, I'm writing a story
about the Tokai regionals.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:53.630
Uh, we're just a no-name school making
our competition debut in Category B.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.260
Relax.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:00.090
Shimizu Minami High School
will easily progress to regionals.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:04.330
There are twenty-six schools
taking part in Category B.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:09.090
Last year, all ten schools that
got gold went to regionals.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:11.160
There's no dud gold in this competition.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.970
Don't say it like that!

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:18.290
Sure, if we can get gold, we'll progress further,

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.950
but we don't know if we can.

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:25.080
Aren't you underestimating your band?

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.250
I've heard you guys perform before,

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:32.500
via a video of the joint performance
you put on in Shimizu.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:36.720
I was amazed he could teach
a no-name band to be that good.

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:40.720
That's Kusakabe Shinjirou for you.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.530
You know of Kusakabe-sensei?

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:48.130
Up until five years ago, he was known as
the wunderkind of the classical music world.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:53.560
Even in a world that produces amazing talent every year,
he was head and shoulders above the rest.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:58.710
Kusakabe Shinjirou, who abandoned a
glittering career and vanished without a trace,

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:03.770
is now trying to stand in the spotlight again
as the instructor of a no-name band.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:07.050
Who wouldn't be interested in a story like that?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:12.050
If I could talk to him directly,
I wouldn't be chasing you kids around.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:16.230
Besides, Fujigasaki's Sakai-sensei
or whoever has made arrangements

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:19.380
to prevent the media from
talking to students at the venue.

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:23.480
Why won't you leave him be?

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.970
Because Kusakabe Shinjirou is the
type of man to leave you kids all alone

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:29.100
on the day of your performance.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.000
Some leader he is.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.040
Get lost.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.690
And don't speak about him like that!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.860
W-Wait a second!

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:45.620
I don't like how you've been talking to Chika-chan,
pure and innocent as she is.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.030
Haruta!

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:47.540
And...

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:49.660
The king of the jungle?!

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:50.650
It's a dog.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:51.910
Talk about huge!

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:56.600
Oh, you're the horn player who's
awfully good at hand-stopping.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:59.210
Could you stop unsettling my bandmate?

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:01.680
We have to perform soon.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.480
Thanks to that Sakai-sensei,

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:07.110
it seems there'll be a ban
on interviews in the afternoon.

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:10.660
So I wanted to talk to you guys while I still could.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:13.100
Why don't we make a deal?

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.880
I found this lost dog here in the morning.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:19.930
Look for its owner.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:22.580
I'm sure it'll make for a fine replacement story.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:26.740
Is this poochy that great?

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:28.880
It's a Tibetan Mastiff.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:30.450
Chibe-tan?

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:32.260
Tibetan Mastiff.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:36.960
They're still largely unknown in Japan,
but it's a breed of dog originating from Tibet.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:42.080
It's considered one of the two top military breeds,
along with the German Shepherd.

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:45.580
A purebred can fetch
seven- to eight-figure sums.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:48.120
What? This dog is worth that much?

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:51.890
You'll be with me forever.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:57.350
Let's be on our way, before the snow falls
and the angels come to take you away.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:01.770
You disgust me!

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:03.360
Are you doing this for money?!

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:06.010
He's gonna live with me!

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:10.590
I mean, I might have to spend my entire life alone.

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:13.400
So I figured I could have him support me!

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:16.500
What in the world is he talking about?

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.710
Pay him no heed. He's a money-grubber.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:25.930
We'll leave this amazing dog with you,
so please find his owner quickly.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:26.800
There he is!

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.350
That's my dog.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.790
Huh? The owner showed up all by himself!

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:35.310
What a relief. So he was here.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:39.690
That's my... dog.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.560
Another owner appeared?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.750
Two owners?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.010
You guys found him.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:51.200
Hand him over to whomever
you believe to be his real owner.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.500
This looks amusing, so I'll watch how it plays out.

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:58.040
A modern day Judgement of Solomon, eh?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:01.990
This is the kind of article that's worthy of a deal.

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:11.430
Every school was really good.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.280
It's fine. Que sera, sera.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:17.240
Once we're done eating,
let's move to the practice space.

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:19.440
Kusakabe-sensei still isn't here.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:23.000
Homura-san and Kamijou-kun aren't back either.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.190
Want me to go look for them?

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:26.480
Sounds like a good idea.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:27.660
I'll go.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.740
You shouldn't split up any further.

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.330
Which one of you is the owner?

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:36.340
I am.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.290
I am...

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:42.630
As if you could ever have a pet this big.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.540
Finders keepers!

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:47.430
I'm not handing him over unless you
have proof that you really are his owner.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.920
He's gonna live with me!

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:51.180
You're still going on about that?

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.930
How much more are you
going to disgrace yourself?

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:58.100
Tell me, who's your real owner?

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:01.280
Hey.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:06.030
I only got him recently,
so he hasn't taken to me yet.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:09.110
He's not used to me yet.

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:10.840
I see.

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:11.740
Oh, I know!

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:15.590
The real owner should have his walk byproducts.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:17.490
I do. Right here.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.050
Here.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:21.160
Go check, Haruta.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:22.320
I have to check?

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:26.470
Step on it. I'll overlook your
disgraceful behaviour from earlier.

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:33.250
How's it look?

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.800
They both have feces with
the same dog fur on them.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.500
We're back to square one.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.740
Practice will start soon...

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:50.690
But among these two is at least
one liar who tried to steal the dog.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:53.290
We can't leave things like this.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.410
Wow, this place is huge!

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:00.440
Thanks for letting us use your
practice area and your instruments.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:03.380
No problem. We've finished
our performance already.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:04.470
And we owe you a lot.

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:05.960
Let's perform like we do all the time.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.670
You have one hour to practise,
until the instruments arrive.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:10.310
Okay!

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:13.670
What's keeping Homura-san and Kamijou-kun?

00:15:13.670 --> 00:15:16.760
I just hope they haven't gotten
themselves in some kind of a mess.

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:20.550
Didn't you get a pedigree when you bought him?

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:22.710
No, I didn't.

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:24.810
I got him from a friend.

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:26.450
What's a pedigree?

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:28.120
Look, Chika-chan.

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:30.570
There's a lock on his collar.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:31.990
A lock?

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.860
I wonder if it's a message saying
not to remove the collar.

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.400
Pie... Simata?

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:39.820
Pie, maybe?

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:41.720
Like in strawberry pie.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:44.230
Pie is his name.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:45.290
Is it?

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:49.200
I don't remember his name.

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:52.810
Mum gave him a difficult one.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:54.880
What's Simata, then?

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:57.530
Oh, that?

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:58.930
It's the previous owner's surname.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:01.430
He's a friend of mine.

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:03.510
So the previous owner was a Shimata?

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:06.230
Yeah. He's the one who gave me the dog.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:10.030
My mum's surname is Shimata too.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:11.620
Really?

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:13.700
We should just talk to your mother.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.600
Could you call her?

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:17.570
I don't know her number.

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:20.590
It doesn't have to be her mobile phone.
What about a home number?

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:25.000
See, she <i>is</i> lying.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.880
Pie is my dog.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:31.630
This is certainly odd, but I don't think
she's lying to make a quick buck.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:36.850
Since you're so doubtful,
I'll unlock the collar for you as proof.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:40.800
It unlocked!

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:44.770
There. Now you get that I'm his owner, right?

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:53.760
Pie sounds like pi, the mathematical constant.

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:55.400
That is, 3.14.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.150
A number anyone could've guessed.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.690
You doubt me?!

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:03.110
I believe you had plenty of time—

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:08.440
from when I tied this mastiff up in this park
and went to the hall, to when I came back—

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:13.470
to try opening the lock,
go to a pet shop, and pick up feces.

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:15.690
I know that this is out of line,

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:19.230
but if you aren't his real owner,
what you're doing amounts to a crime.

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.920
You weren't kidding about being out of line.

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:24.090
Who are you to talk, anyway?

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:28.490
Why didn't you contact animal control
or the police as soon as you found the dog?

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:31.130
You said you went to the hall,

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:34.470
which means you must be high schoolers
taking part in the concert band competition.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:38.910
I could report you to the organisers
or your school, you know.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:43.710
The number you're trying to call
is currently switched off or—

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:45.120
No go.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:48.850
They probably turned off their phones
when they came into the hall.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:51.730
Let's rehearse in parts until Sensei gets here!

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:52.290
Got it!

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:58.250
Come on, tell me which one is your real owner!

00:17:58.250 --> 00:18:00.470
Bark or woof or something, jeez!

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:04.470
If you don't hand him over now,
I really will contact your school.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.920
Sorry to say, but this is as far as it goes.

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:14.240
In the end, you couldn't find definitive proof
that shows who's the real owner.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.590
The deal is off the table.

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.290
Don't give up!

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:23.250
Not if this is important to you.

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:25.880
Kusakabe-sensei!

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:33.700
Did you two stick your noses
where they didn't belong again?

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:38.310
This is your dog, and he's important to you, right?

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:42.980
Yes. Mum loved him very much.

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:45.110
Your mother?

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:46.930
She let me have him

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.890
when she broke up with Dad.

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:55.590
Did she give you anything else along with him?

00:18:57.300 --> 00:18:58.900
Through the Looking-Glass!

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:00.430
Lewis Carroll?

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:04.610
Yeah. She named him after
something from the book, too.

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:07.910
A difficult name that appears
in Through the Looking-Glass...

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:10.370
Humpty Dumpty?

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:13.430
Tweedledum?

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:14.210
Alice!

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:15.320
Jabberwock?

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.430
That's it! His name's Jabberwock!

00:19:17.430 --> 00:19:22.890
His name was Al before, but she suddenly
changed it before giving him to me.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:26.150
Then the "Pie" on his collar isn't his name?

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:32.360
You don't know how to
contact your mother, right?

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:36.100
Right. Dad said I couldn't see her anymore.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:51.190
Do you have a pocket mirror
on you, Chika-chan?

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.920
Y-Yeah.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:53.960
Look.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:55.920
When you mirror these letters, you get...

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:58.510
ATAMI2 314.

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:00.250
An address?

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:03.610
This might be a dog licence ID number.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.810
If so, you can use this number

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:10.610
to look up the address it was
registered under at animal control.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:14.470
And that might be where your mother is.

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:18.270
ATAMI2 314...

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:24.700
Those are the directions your mother
left you along with this mastiff.

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:31.540
Here you go. Don't let him get lost again.

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:35.550
Let's go see her together someday.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:38.890
Turns out you were the one who was out of line.

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:41.090
Huh? Where'd he go?

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.680
He turned tail and quietly snuck away.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:48.070
What brought this on?

00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:52.320
After what you did,
you still can't let go of your baton?

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:56.210
Music is all I know,

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:58.110
so I cling to it.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:03.670
Well, I did make a deal,
so I'll let you off the hook for today.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.290
I expect great things at
the competition, you hear me?

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:10.840
Here's the phone number for animal control.

00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:14.290
Try calling them once you're out of diapers.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:16.080
Don't tell Pops, though.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:19.700
Is he actually a nice guy?

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.690
Divorce by arbitration.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:25.380
I guess her father won custody of her.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.800
There's no way to tell what happened,

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:32.010
but I'm sure the separated mother was
made to accept some harsh conditions.

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:36.220
She couldn't even give her daughter
her address or contact info.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.740
Breakups can be that cruel, huh?

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:41.320
Found you!

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:43.320
What're you doing here?!

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:45.340
Practice has already started!

00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:46.640
Oh, sorry!

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:49.700
Save the apologies for Narushima-san
after you get back.

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:51.110
Jeez!

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.020
Let's hurry!

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.950
Come on, Haruta, Sensei!

00:21:57.950 --> 00:21:59.120
Shall we, Sensei?

00:21:59.120 --> 00:21:59.740
Yeah.

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:33.660
Your conducting style
sure has changed, Shinjirou!

00:23:33.660 --> 00:23:34.270
Come on!

00:23:34.270 --> 00:23:35.770
Tell me how you really feel, Nao-chan!

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:36.560
You piece of trash!

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:38.650
I'll expose that vixen's true colours!

00:23:38.650 --> 00:23:40.160
Cheeky brat.
